# Tongue - jaw harps: a reed ringing through a slot, and a mouth that picks
# out its harmonics.
#
# The steel harp is fitted to measured recordings (tools/tongue_reference):
# its harmonics close to level up to the 16th, the odd and even about equal,
# the mouth's formants at 0.5 to 1.6 kHz and 1.4 to 3.2 kHz bringing out the
# 3rd to 10th, a pluck falling about 36 dB a second when played 7 times a
# second, its fundamental and 2nd falling at half that. The other kinds come
# in a later part.
#
# Each patch plays the `jaw` phrase: one note plucked in a gallop, the mod
# wheel (the mouth) stepping through vowels, then a pluck left to ring.
# Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Tongue` lists
# them. A patch names only what it changes.
#
# What is still wrong:
#   - Only the steel harp so far; every model plays it.
#   - Breath is set by ear: the recordings were too quick to measure it.
#   - The fit to the recordings' median (tools/tongue_reference/fit.py) is
#     2.4 dB rms over the first twelve harmonics, a ripple every third
#     harmonic from the slot. A real recording against the median of the
#     others is 6.3 dB, the closest 2.6, so this is inside their scatter.

machine Tongue
role    jaw

# --- steel -------------------------------------------------------------------

patch Init family=steel note=55 range=48..67

patch "Bright Steel" family=steel note=55 range=48..67
  # A close-fitting reed flicked hard: every harmonic up, the mouth narrow.
  edge           0.85
  pluck          0.9
  focus          0.85
  volume         0.67

patch "Soft Steel" family=steel note=55 range=48..67
  # Plucked gently with the pad of the finger, the mouth doing more of the work.
  pluck          0.2
  edge           0.35
  ring           4
  depth          0.6
  mouth          0.2
  volume         1.0

patch "Breathing Steel" family=steel note=55 range=48..67
  # Breathed through as it's played, the breath keeping it going.
  breath         0.5
  air            0.5
  sustain        0.6
  volume         0.53
